We continue our genral study of parametrized curves in R³, considering how to measure such geometric properties as length and curvature. 
This can be done by deining three mutually perpendicular unit vectors that form the so-called moving frame specially adapted to a path x. 
Our study takes us briefly into the branch of mathematics called differential geometry, and area where calculus and analysis are used to understand the geometry of curves, surfaces, and certain heigher-dimensional objects (called manifolds)
